==id $Id: openmaketask_lib.sfd 1.0 (17.11.2026) $
* "openmaketask.library": work spread over the machine's cores (gs_par.h),
* for every OpenMake program: n pieces, each the program's own function,
* run once each on exec tasks, the call returning when all have. Each call
* is its C function in snake case (GS_ParRun is gs_par_run). Never
* reorder or take a call out; add new ones at the end.
* core/library/gen-library.py writes the rest from this.
==base _OpenMakeTaskBase
==basetype struct Library *
==libname openmaketask.library
==bias 30
==public
==include <exec/types.h>
==include <gs_par.h>
int GS_ParRun(int n, gs_par_fn fn, void *arg)(d0,a0,a1)
int GS_ParCores()()
==end
